void unit_test_insert_null_tree(void) {
    // Setup: no tree exists
    struct node* root = NULL;
    int key = 42;

    // Test: insert into empty tree
    struct node* result = insert(root, key);

    // Assertions
    assert(result != NULL);
    assert(result->key == 42);
    assert(result->left == NULL);
    assert(result->right == NULL);

    // Cleanup
    free(result);
}
```

SUCCESS CRITERIA:
- Test exercises the target path with correct inputs
- All function calls exist in operation map or standard C library
- Memory properly managed (no leaks)
- Assertions verify expected behavior
- Code compiles without errors
- Test function name is descriptive: unit_test_<function>_<scenario>

Output ONLY the C test function code. No explanations, no JSON, just compilable C code.

Generate a C test function for the following execution path.

FUNCTION UNDER TEST:
Name: deleteNode
Signature: struct node* deleteNode(struct node* root, int key)
Description: /**
 * @brief Remove a node with a given key from a binary search tree.
 *
 * Deletes the node containing the specified key from the BST rooted at root,
 * maintaining BST ordering. If the key is not found, the tree is unchanged.
 * Handles all cases: node with zero, one, or two children.
 *
 * @param root Root of the BST, or NULL for an empty tree. Caller retains ownership.
 * @param key Key to remove from the tree.
 *
 * @return Root of the modified tree. Returns NULL if the tree becomes empty.
 *
 * @note Memory: Frees the removed node. Caller must free the final tree.
 * @see minValueNode
 */
Dependencies: deleteNode, minValueNode

FUNCTION IMPLEMENTATION:
```c
// C program for the function called deleteNode
// Contains target function implementation and dependency signatures

#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>

struct node {
	int key;
	struct node *left, *right;
};

// Forward declarations for dependency functions
struct node* minValueNode(struct node* node);

// Target function implementation
struct node* deleteNode(struct node* root, int key)
{

	if (root == NULL)
		return root;


	if (key < root->key)
		root->left = deleteNode(root->left, key);


	else if (key > root->key)
		root->right = deleteNode(root->right, key);


	else {
		if (root->left == NULL) {
			struct node* temp = root->right;
			free(root);
			return temp;
		}
		else if (root->right == NULL) {
			struct node* temp = root->left;
			free(root);
			return temp;
		}

		struct node* temp = minValueNode(root->right);


		root->key = temp->key;

		root->right = deleteNode(root->right, temp->key);
	}
	return root;
}

```

